From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lunfan Zhang <Lunfan.Zhang@cloud.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 06:27:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CA-432792: Tag the mirror leaf VDI through the destination's
 SMAPI

receive_start_common runs on the source host when called through
receive_start3, with SMAPI bound to the destination host's storage API.
The leaf VDI is created there, but its tags were added through Local,
the source host's own storage mux, which has no plugin for the
destination SR. Every SXM of a tagged VDI to an SR not plugged on the
source host, including all cross-pool migrations, failed with
No_storage_plugin_for_sr.

Add the tags through SMAPI, like every other operation on the leaf.

Signed-off-by: Lunfan Zhang <Lunfan.Zhang@cloud.com>
(cherry picked from commit a416d1d0589ae5fa1282944019fab6b47dc0959f)
---
 ocaml/xapi/storage_smapiv1_migrate.ml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ocaml/xapi/storage_smapiv1_migrate.ml b/ocaml/xapi/storage_smapiv1_migrate.ml
index b8d43ee79..0031f6125 100644
--- a/ocaml/xapi/storage_smapiv1_migrate.ml
+++ b/ocaml/xapi/storage_smapiv1_migrate.ml
@@ -652,7 +652,7 @@ module MIRROR : SMAPIv2_MIRROR = struct
       let leaf = SMAPI.VDI.create dbg sr vdi_info in
 
       List.iter
-        (fun tag -> Local.VDI.add_tags dbg sr leaf.vdi tag)
+        (fun tag -> SMAPI.VDI.add_tags dbg sr leaf.vdi tag)
         vdi_info.tags ;
 
       D.info "Created leaf VDI for mirror receive: %s" (string_of_vdi_info leaf) ;
